            <h2>Route Overview: Alexandria to New York </h2>
            <p>Traveling from Alexandria to New York by train is a convenient and scenic way to connect Northern Virginia with the nation's largest metropolitan hub. This route offers passengers a relaxed alternative to driving or flying, especially popular with business travelers, students, tourists, and weekend travelers. While not as fast as high-speed rail in Europe, the Acela Express offers America's fastest train service, reaching up to 150 mph, with comfortable seating, onboard amenities, and spectacular views along the Northeast Corridor. </p>
            <p>The route is served by Amtrak's Acela Express, Northeast Regional, Carolinian, and Palmetto, offering multiple daily departures between Alexandria Union Station and New York Penn Station (Moynihan Train Hall). Compared to road travel on the congested I-95 corridor, taking the train helps you avoid highway traffic. It makes city-center-to-city-center travel easy in Manhattan without worrying about parking or tolls. </p>
