            <h2>Train Duration, Distance, and Travel Time Overview</h2>
            <p>Traveling from Alexandria to New York covers roughly 208-232 miles (335-374 km) along the Northeast Corridor, linking Northern Virginia with the nation's largest city. This is one of Amtrak's busiest and most popular routes, with the Acela Express offering America's fastest train service and the Northeast Regional providing a more economical alternative. </p>
