            <h3>What This Means for Travelers</h3>
            <p>Taking the train between Alexandria and New York gives you a moderately long, productive travel experience. It's often comparable to flying when factoring in airport time, but allows you to relax, use Wi-Fi, stretch your legs, and enjoy views of the Atlantic coastline, historic cities, and the Chesapeake Bay. Compared to road travel, the train avoids I-95 traffic stress and delivers you straight into Manhattan's Penn Station without needing a car. </p>
            <h4>Key Points: </h4>
            <ul>
                <li>Perfect for business trips, weekend getaways, or tourism with multiple daily departures throughout the day.</li>
                <li>Traveling by train allows you to work, read, or simply enjoy the scenery along one of America's most historic rail corridors.</li>
                <li>Consistent schedules ensure predictable travel planning, with trains running from early morning (3:00 AM) to late evening (9:00 PM).</li>
                <li>The Acela Express offers first-class amenities comparable to business-class air travel, while the Northeast Regional provides budget-friendly options starting at just $34.</li>
            </ul>
